<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>API Documentation | Hudson Street Library</title>
    <meta name="description" content="Programmatic access to Hudson Street Library catalog data via standard RFC 9727 API discovery">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/tailwind.css">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/css/design-system.css">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="/favicon-32x32.png">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="/favicon-16x16.png">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
    {% include "components/api-catalog-link.njk" %}
</head>
<body class="min-h-screen bg-neutral-50 text-neutral-900">

{% include "components/site-header.njk" %}

<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-6">API Documentation</h1>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Discovery</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">Hudson Street Library implements <a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc9727/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">RFC 9727</a> for API discovery. You can discover the available APIs in two ways:</p>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Well-Known URI</h3>
    <pre class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-sm mb-4 overflow-x-auto"><code>GET {{ site.url }}/.well-known/api-catalog</code></pre>

    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Link Relations</h3>
    <p class="mb-2">Each HTML page includes this link element:</p>
    <pre class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-sm mb-4 overflow-x-auto"><code>&lt;link rel="api-catalog" type="application/linkset+json" href="/.well-known/api-catalog"&gt;</code></pre>

    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4"><strong>Note:</strong> HTTP Link headers are not available because GitHub Pages does not support custom response headers. The well-known URI and the HTML link element work.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Available APIs</h2>

    <div class="border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-4 mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Full Catalog JSON</h3>
      <p class="mb-2"><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">{{ site.url }}/data/books.json</code></p>
      <p class="mb-2">This endpoint returns the complete published catalog of {{ publishedBooks.length }} book records, regenerated on every deployment.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2"><strong>Format:</strong> application/json</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Schema:</strong> <a href="/schemas/book-collection/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">/schemas/book-collection/</a></p>

      <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Example:</h4>
      <pre class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>curl {{ site.url }}/data/books.json | jq '.[0]'</code></pre>
    </div>

    <div class="border-l-4 border-green-500 pl-4 mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">CSV Export</h3>
      <p class="mb-2"><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">{{ site.url }}/cms/data/books.csv</code></p>
      <p class="mb-2">This endpoint returns the art wing as CSV. Each record has 37 columns.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2"><strong>Format:</strong> text/csv</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Schema:</strong> <a href="/schemas/book-csv/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">/schemas/book-csv/</a></p>

      <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Example:</h4>
      <pre class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>curl {{ site.url }}/cms/data/books.csv | head -5</code></pre>

      <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Every wing:</h4>
      <p class="mb-2"><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">{{ site.url }}/cms/data/catalog.csv</code></p>
      <p class="mb-2">The same 37 columns with a 38th, <code class="bg-gray-100 px-1 rounded-sm">collection</code>, naming the wing each record belongs to. This is the file the catalogue page itself reads.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="border-l-4 border-purple-500 pl-4 mb-6">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-2">Collections Metadata</h3>
      <p class="mb-2"><code class="bg-gray-100 px-2 py-1 rounded-sm">{{ site.url }}/cms/data/libraryCollections.json</code></p>
      <p class="mb-2">This endpoint returns the thematic collection groupings.</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-2"><strong>Format:</strong> application/json</p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-600"><strong>Schema:</strong> <a href="/schemas/collections/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">/schemas/collections/</a></p>

      <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">Example:</h4>
      <pre class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-sm overflow-x-auto"><code>curl {{ site.url }}/cms/data/libraryCollections.json | jq '.'</code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Rate Limits & Usage</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">GitHub Pages serves all endpoints as static files. No rate limits apply beyond the standard GitHub CDN throttling. When the library adds new books, the next deployment updates the data.</p>

    <p class="mb-4"><strong>CORS:</strong> All endpoints support cross-origin requests.</p>

    <p class="mb-4"><strong>Caching:</strong> GitHub Pages serves the files with standard HTTP cache headers. The catalog usually updates weekly.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Standards Compliance</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc9727/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">RFC 9727</a> - API Catalog Format and Discovery</li>
      <li><a href="https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/rfc9264/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">RFC 9264</a> - Linkset: Media Types and a Link Relation Type</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/json-ld11/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">JSON-LD 1.1</a> - Individual book pages include Schema.org structured data</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">Questions?</h2>
    <p>To ask a question about the API or to report a problem, open an issue on the <a href="https://github.com/Mediaeater/Hudson_Street_Library" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">project repository</a>.</p>
  </section>
</div>

{% include "components/site-footer.njk" %}

</body>
</html>
